From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx8-isi-cap: tolerate optional get_frame_interval

mxc_isi_cap_g_parm() treats negative return from v4l2_g_parm_cap() as a
failure, including -ENOIOCTLCMD, which simply means the sensor does not
implement that optional op. Tolerate -ENOIOCTLCMD so VIDIOC_G_PARM no
longer fails just because the sensor does not report an explicit frame
interval.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate NXP proprietary driver
---
 drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
index 5d8bb442fa56..9385d2fc76bb 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
@@ -1072,10 +1072,14 @@ static int mxc_isi_cap_g_parm(struct file *file, void *fh,
 {
 	struct mxc_isi_cap_dev *isi_cap = video_drvdata(file);
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sd;
+	int ret;
 
 	sd = mxc_get_remote_subdev(&isi_cap->sd, __func__);
 	if (!sd)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	return v4l2_g_parm_cap(video_devdata(file), sd, a);
+	ret = v4l2_g_parm_cap(video_devdata(file), sd, a);
+	if (ret == -ENOIOCTLCMD)
+		return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int mxc_isi_cap_s_parm(struct file *file, void *fh,
